Chapter: BvtHttpLength
  cites Net chapter WebServer
  cites Works chapter Http
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 The admin port's HTTP framing reads Content-Length before any key is checked: a 20-digit length multiplied past the
 Integer range, and an overflowing multiply traps, so one unauthenticated request halted the shard (val, UOAIX audit
 2026-10-18). A length past the receive buffer now only never completes.
  bhl-request : Text, List Integer -> List Integer
  bhl-request (length) (body) = http-text-to-ascii "POST /admin HTTP/1.1" & [13, 10] & http-text-to-ascii ("Content-Length: " & length) & [13, 10, 13, 10] & body
  bhl-total : Text, List Integer -> Integer
  bhl-total (length) (body) = let bytes = bhl-request length body in wb-request-total bytes (list-length bytes)
  bvt-http-length : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-http-length (unused) = let whole = bhl-request "3" [97, 98, 99]
    in let fits = bhl-total "3" [97, 98, 99] == list-length whole
    in let short = bhl-total "4" [97, 98, 99] == -1
    in let huge = bhl-total "99999999999999999999" [97, 98, 99] == -1
    in let wide = bhl-total "999999999999999999999999999999999999999999" [] == -1
    in act
    a <- bvt-check "a request whose Content-Length its body meets is framed whole, and one a byte short waits" (fits & short)
    b <- bvt-check "a 20-digit and a 42-digit Content-Length are a request that never completes, not a trap" (huge & wide)
    a + b
  end
